              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">TTL</span>
                <span id="resultTtl" class="result-value">
                  300 seconds
                </span>
              </div>

              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">Record Name</span>
                <span id="resultName" class="result-value">
                  www.example.com.
                </span>
              </div>

              <div class="result-item">
                <span class="result-label">DNS Class</span>
                <span class="result-value">IN</span>
              </div>

              <div class="result-item full">
                <span class="result-label">Record Value</span>
                <span id="resultValue" class="result-value">
                  192.0.2.10
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="explanation">
              <h3>Record explanation</h3>

              <ul
                id="explanationList"
                class="explanation-list"
              ></ul>
            </div>

            <div class="warning">
              DNS provider forms differ. Some providers expect only the short
              host name, while others expect a complete domain name. Verify the
              generated record before publishing it.
